# Line endings that are load-bearing, not a style preference.
#
# The legacy BIO driver package's catalogue (built by
# packaging/net2860_winusb/build_driver_package.ps1, gitignored) hashes the
# INF's *bytes*. Without a rule here, git rewrites that file to whatever the
# local core.autocrlf happens to say, so an ordinary checkout or branch
# switch can silently invalidate an already-signed catalogue.
#
# That is not hypothetical: it happened on 2026-09-10 and surfaced only on a
# clinic machine, as `pnputil` exit code -536870325 (0xE000024B,
# SPAPI_E_FILE_HASH_NOT_IN_CATALOG) during install. Pinning the working-tree
# form makes the checked-out bytes identical on every machine regardless of
# local git config, which is what the catalogue needs. See DECISIONS.md.
*.inf text eol=crlf
